nergy consumption  looking ahead to what the techniques are  for  carbon um footprint aware software  development  something i find as a software developer  in in doing  profiling of things one of the real big  principles that you run into  and and what you run into in practice is  knowing what you're actually measuring  you know  if you if you're measuring you know cpu  cycle or  memory usage of something it's  when you do the measurement are you  actually measuring the thing that you  have  that you can make an impact on um so  thinking about that what are your  thoughts about  how what metrics there would be to  see that you're improving things and  then how do you actually  do the measuring on that that's a great  question  and that's actually what i aspire to do  as part of you know my job where today  when you write code  you have unit tests that catch your bugs  and you have integration tests so you  you deploy your code there are a bunch  of tests that run and then you know that  whether it's good or not  and i aspire to make a framework where  you know it's not just  uh functionally correct code but  environmentally  good code so you will have a framework  or a series of tests that you can run  that like you said measure the memory  usage measure the cpu cycles of your  code  measure the amount of spin spinning of  your like if you have spin locks  anywhere or  uh detecting those kind of things in  your code and give you alternatives  for those also stuff what compilers do  these days right  loop unrolling uh some of these things  that you can do on your end i think  these would be good starting points  and then you can use a lot of static  analysis tools that are already  available in coding so  they would be a great starting point and  then uh like you said you know flame  graphs are a good way to know which  function is being hit the most  and you can then get into that like  which particular function needs to be  optimized the most  for energy so those 